      "bank": { "instruments": ["lead-bright", "harm-soft", "pluck", "bass", "bass-short", "tri-kick", "kick", "snare", "tom", "hat-closed", "hat-open", "crash"], "rev": 1 },
      "percussionGap": 8,
      "notes": "POLYMETER (structural): the triangle's 16th engine carries a 3-ROW register cell (two low, one octave-up) written straight through the bar lines, so the octave accent rotates 3-against-4 and only realigns every 3 bars — tri:0/1/2 put the high note on rows where r%3==2, tri:3 phase-shifts it to r%3==0 (frame 3:0 onward) which is the same cell displaced. B swaps it for a TRESILLO bass (3+3+2 eighths: rows 0/6/12 of every bar, frames 8-11), and A' answers with a tresillo KICK (rows 0/6/12, frames 6-7 noise:4) under a straight backbeat. HEMIOLA at the last cadence: pulse 1 and pulse 2 group by 3 rows from frame 16 row 32 to row 59 across a 16-row bar. METRIC EVENT: D00 on noise:7 row 47 cuts the break to 3 bars (frame 12), so A'' arrives a bar early; frame 12 rows 25-31 are a deliberate dropped beat with the whole kit out. RHYTHMIC DISPLACEMENT: the motif is restated one row late in p1:3 and two rows late in p1:4, and re-orchestrated onto pulse 2 in frame 6 (p2:4). Fast broken-chord arp run on `pluck` as the transition into A'' (frame 12 rows 32-47). HARMONY: A = i-bVII-IV-i then i-bVI-bVII-v (B flat = borrowed colour 1); B is a 6-bar chromatic bass descent d-c#-c-b-bb-a (Dm - A7/c# - Dm7/c - G/b - Bb - Am) plus a 2-bar link, the 6-bar phrase being the piece's asymmetry, and it closes F -> A, a chromatic mediant, into the break's dominant pedal; A'' ends on the chained secondary dominants E7 (g#) -> A7 (c#) -> Dm across the loop seam. Suspensions: 4-3 on pulse 2 over G (p2:2 rows 32/40), 7-6 over A7 (p2:5 rows 24/32). DECIMAL PARAMS: Q param 50 = Q32 = note-slide up 2 semitones at speed 3; Q param 117 = Q75; R param 51 = R33 = fall 3 semitones; 2 param 0 = 200, which is the ONLY way to cancel a Qxy/Rxy on this engine (300 does not cancel, it freezes portamento) and it is placed before every note that must retrigger; 0 param 55 = 037 minor triad, 71 = 047 major triad, 74 = 04a dominant 7; A param 3 = A03 swell UP (Axy is inverted here: x fades, y swells), 32 = A20 fade; G param 2/3 = 2- and 3-tick flams; D param 0 = D00. rmsRange is declared because the design's [-20,-9] window is unreachable on this engine; -20.5 dBFS measured, declared [-24,-17]. Accidentals are 11.1% of melodic events, inside Gate B's 12%, and every one of them is a named colour (bb, c#, g#, d#) rather than drift."
